# Android app support.
# Waydroid runs a real Android system image in a container on the host kernel,
# so it needs binder support (binder_linux) and a Wayland session. The setup
# script checks both and refuses cleanly instead of corrupting the session.
# waydroid ships only in trixie-backports/main; the android hook installs it
# with `apt-get install -t trixie-backports` and configures binder_linux.
^waydroid
# Optional companion tools
?waydroid-image-gapps
?weston
?adbd
